\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.2 Long-press behavior \'97 critical requirement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Long-pressing the Loop button must open the 
\f0\b Custom Loop Editor
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A long press must not accidentally trigger the short-tap cycle.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The editor must offer Off, Finite Section Loop, and Infinite Section Loop.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The user must be able to select the section manually or use Auto Loop.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Existing saved loop settings must be loaded when appropriate.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The editor must provide clear Save/Apply and Cancel actions.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cancelling must not overwrite the previous saved configuration.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 3.3 Interaction consistency\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use familiar playback icons and standard tap behavior.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Provide visual feedback for the current repeat mode.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Show an obvious indication when a custom section loop is active.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use accessible touch targets and readable text.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ensure the long-press gesture works reliably on supported iPhones.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Do not require the user to open a settings screen for everyday repeat behavior.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Music Library\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 FR-001 \'97 Import music:
\f1\b0  Import supported local audio files through the iOS Files picker. Support MP3 and M4A/AAC, and WAV where supported by the playback stack.\

\f0\b FR-002 \'97 Persistent storage:
\f1\b0  Copy imported audio into app-managed storage so files remain available after the original Files location changes.\

\f0\b FR-003 \'97 Library browsing:
\f1\b0  Provide Songs, Albums, Artists, Playlists, Recently Played, and Favorites views.\

\f0\b FR-004 \'97 Search:
\f1\b0  Search the local library by song title, artist, album, and other available metadata.\

\f0\b FR-005 \'97 Metadata:
\f1\b0  Display title, artist, album artwork, and duration where available. Provide reasonable fallbacks for missing metadata.\

\f0\b FR-006 \'97 Library management:
\f1\b0  Allow users to remove songs from the library, with clear confirmation where removal could delete the stored audio file.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Standard Playback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 FR-007 \'97 Playback controls:
\f1\b0  Provide Play/Pause, Previous, Next, seek bar, elapsed time, and total duration.\

\f0\b FR-008 \'97 Queue:
\f1\b0  Provide a queue view, with predictable Next and Previous behavior.\

\f0\b FR-009 \'97 Background playback:
\f1\b0  Continue audio during screen lock and while the app is backgrounded, subject to iOS system behavior.\

\f0\b FR-010 \'97 System media controls:
\f1\b0  Integrate with Now Playing, the lock screen, Control Centre, and supported headphone media controls.\

\f0\b FR-011 \'97 Playback persistence:
\f1\b0  Preserve the current song and sensible playback position across interruptions and app restarts.\

\f0\b FR-012 \'97 Audio interruptions:
\f1\b0  Handle calls, other audio sessions, headphone disconnection, and audio-session interruptions gracefully.\

\f0\b FR-013 \'97 Seeking:
\f1\b0  Manual seeking must not leave playback stuck, cause duplicate loop transitions, or trigger stale loop callbacks.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 6. Custom Section Looping\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 FR-014 \'97 Select a region:
\f1\b0  Let the user choose a start and end position within a song.\

\f0\b FR-015 \'97 Finite section loop:
\f1\b0  Repeat the selected region for a user-configured number of total plays in the looping sequence, then continue playback from the end of the selected region by default.\

\f0\b FR-016 \'97 Infinite section loop:
\f1\b0  Repeat the selected region indefinitely, without an automatic repeat limit or automatic exit.\

\f0\b FR-017 \'97 Explicit exit behavior:
\f1\b0  An infinite section loop must exit when the user explicitly presses Next through the in-app button, lock-screen/Now Playing controls, Control Centre, or supported headphone media controls. The user must also be able to disable the custom loop explicitly.\

\f0\b FR-018 \'97 Track-specific configuration:
\f1\b0  Save loop start, loop end, loop mode, repeat count, and other relevant settings per song.\

\f0\b FR-019 \'97 Persistent profiles:
\f1\b0  Switching to another song must not erase the previous song's saved configuration. Replaying a song should restore its saved loop configuration.\

\f0\b FR-020 \'97 Separate saved and transient state:
\f1\b0  Keep the saved loop profile separate from the current playback position, repeat counter, and active looping session.\

\f0\b FR-021 \'97 Finite loop completion:
\f1\b0  After the configured number of plays, exit the section loop exactly once and continue from the loop end. Do not accidentally re-enter the loop because of a stale playback-position event.\

\f0\b FR-022 \'97 Next-track priority:
\f1\b0  A Next command must cancel pending loop transitions, terminate the current looping session, advance the queue, and load the next track's own saved profile. An infinite loop must never block Next.\

\f0\b FR-023 \'97 Pause and resume:
\f1\b0  Pause and resume must preserve the selected section, repeat count progress, and current mode.\

\f0\b FR-024 \'97 Loop validation:
\f1\b0  Reject or correct invalid ranges, including a start position at or after the end position and regions outside the song duration.\

\f0\b FR-025 \'97 Loop indicators:
\f1\b0  Display whether the current mode is whole-song repeat or custom section repeat. For finite loops, show remaining repetitions when useful; for infinite loops, display an infinity indicator.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 7. Waveform Editor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 FR-026 \'97 Waveform display:
\f1\b0  Render a waveform for the current track or selected region.\

\f0\b FR-027 \'97 Draggable handles:
\f1\b0  Provide distinct start and end handles with timestamps.\

\f0\b FR-028 \'97 Precision adjustment:
\f1\b0  Support fine adjustments targeting approximately 100 ms where the audio engine and seeking accuracy permit. Do not promise sample-accurate editing unless verified.\

\f0\b FR-029 \'97 Preview:
\f1\b0  Allow users to preview the selected region before saving.\

\f0\b FR-030 \'97 Boundary adjustments:
\f1\b0  Allow users to move either boundary without unintentionally moving the other.\

\f0\b FR-031 \'97 Waveform caching:
\f1\b0  Cache generated waveform data where practical to reduce repeated processing.\

\f0\b FR-032 \'97 Editing feedback:
\f1\b0  Clearly indicate the selected region and prevent handles from crossing into an invalid range.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 8. Auto Loop\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 FR-033 \'97 Target duration:
\f1\b0  Let the user specify a desired loop duration, with a sensible default and configurable range.\

\f0\b FR-034 \'97 Selection preferences:
\f1\b0  Offer musically aligned, energy-based, and exact-duration selection preferences where practical.\

\f0\b FR-035 \'97 Candidate analysis:
\f1\b0  Use audio features such as short-time energy, onset strength, beat estimates, boundary similarity, and phrase coherence to identify potential loop points.\

\f0\b FR-036 \'97 Candidate preview:
\f1\b0  Present a suggested region with adjustable handles and a preview action.\

\f0\b FR-037 \'97 Apply confirmation:
\f1\b0  Never overwrite an existing saved loop profile without user confirmation.\

\f0\b FR-038 \'97 Honest feedback:
\f1\b0  If no good candidate is found, explain that result and allow manual selection. Do not claim perfect musical transitions.\

\f0\b FR-039 \'97 Processing states:
\f1\b0  Show loading, success, and failure states with a retry option.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 9. Now Playing UI\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 FR-040 \'97 Main layout:
\f1\b0  Include artwork, track information, seek bar, playback controls, and the Loop button.\

\f0\b FR-041 \'97 Loop button placement:
\f1\b0  Make the Loop button easy to reach without crowding primary playback controls.\

\f0\b FR-042 \'97 Active state:
\f1\b0  Distinguish Off, Repeat once, Repeat infinitely, Finite section loop, and Infinite section loop visually.\

\f0\b FR-043 \'97 Custom editor entry:
\f1\b0  Long-press the Loop button to open the Custom Loop Editor. Also provide a discoverable alternative entry point for users who do not know the gesture.\

\f0\b FR-044 \'97 Mini-player:
\f1\b0  Show the current track and playback status while navigating the library.\

\f0\b FR-045 \'97 Navigation:
\f1\b0  Provide library, search, Now Playing, and queue navigation without unnecessarily interrupting playback.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

